  "hypurrt": {
    "token": "0xff6a3387cf21ef2ed2e94da324bce290ca9abc3b",
    "text": "What is reassuring\n\nNo sale and no liquidity removal by the creator was observed, and the creator's transfers reached none of the holders read. The creator's 3.99% launch-block purchase was sent to a burn address. Outside pools, locks and burn addresses, no wallet holds more than 4.10%. The creator's wallet was first funded by a routing contract, which links it to nobody.\n\nWhat deserves attention\n\nIn the first 10 minutes, 106 early buyers bought 73.80% of the supply in total, and 190 addresses bought and sold back within that window. The trading rules (hook) can alter any trade, including taking a cut of a sell or stopping it, and what they actually do is not readable. The same hook serves 10320 markets, which may just be a launchpad standard. Three other liquidity providers took back their own positions, which is separate from the creator's liquidity.\n\nWhere the signals diverge\n\nToday's holder list looks spread out, yet the launch window shows heavy buying and quick resale: early buyers still hold 11.44% of what they bought, 11 of those addresses could not be read. Holders look dispersed partly because many early buyers have left. The creator's record shows no sale, but only one launch was found on the launchpads SEAL can list, so there is little history to judge. The report is partial: only 3 pages of holders were read, distinct traders were not collected, and only the standard upgrade slot was checked on the hook, so later rule changes are not ruled out.",
