  "wheelSmith": {
    "token": "0xeb579e280648b6f48a840086a9e6631500a20684",
    "text": "What is reassuring\n\nThe holder read covered only 3 pages, so it is partial. Sells are going through: 1714 sells against 2037 buys in 24 hours. The creator's first funder is a high-volume service, which says nothing about who is behind the wallet.\n\nWhat deserves attention\n\nThe creator sold this token into its market, and it sold back 3.23% within the first 10 minutes. Whether it removed liquidity could not be read this time, so the report is partial on that point. A third of the supply sits in pools and launch contracts, so only 67% circulates. In the first 10 minutes, 38 addresses bought and then sold back. The 9 early buyers bought 25.28% of the supply and hold 0.49% today.\n\nWhere the signals diverge\n\nThe current picture looks broad: 1550 holder addresses, modest top holdings, and 464,640 USD of 24-hour volume. The launch window looks different, with many quick round trips and creator sales. Today's holder spread says little about who traded in those first minutes. The volume read also did not collect distinct traders, so how many separate people produce today's trading cannot be concluded. The trading rules (hook) can alter trade amounts, though what they do is not readable. No standard upgrade slot is set on them, but the token's own contract was not checked. No other launch was found on the launchpads SEAL can list, which leaves the creator's wider record unknown."
  },
  "asteroid": {
    "token": "0xfd82d8db539b6ace0d50815845133767e24f1e18",
    "text": "What is reassuring\n\nLiquidity is about 199,000 USD, and no liquidity removal by the creator was observed on this token in its first 11 days. Outside pools and contracts, the largest holder has 4.43% and there are 2966 holder addresses. The hook code has no standard upgrade slot set, though only that one pattern was checked.\n\nWhat deserves attention\n\nThe creator sold this token over its 96 days so far, and sold on 7 of 9 other launches in their first 11 days. It also took 6.91% of supply as trading fees in 52 transfers. It sent tokens to 6 addresses outside markets, and one contract passed 3.94% on to 105 addresses. The first funder of the creator's wallet bought at +17 s and sold back at +115 s. Only 79.09% of supply circulates outside pools and contracts.\n\nWhere the signals diverge\n\nYet the early record points the other way. 17 early buyers bought 17.94% of supply and now hold 0.00%, and 18 addresses bought and sold back within the window. Several creator recipients, including the funder, also appear among the early buyers. A transfer links addresses but does not show who controls them. The holder read covers 3 pages only, graduation was not determined, and distinct traders in the 24-hour volume were not collected, so the data cannot say who drives today's trading."
